System.out.println(name); // Tuesday
```
Classic switch needs `break` in every case; arrow switch implicitly breaks after each one.

```java
int day = 6;
String type;
switch (day) {
    case 1: case 2: case 3: case 4: case 5:
        type = "Weekday"; break;  // shared block — intentional fall-through
    case 6: case 7:
        type = "Weekend"; break;
    default:
        type = "Invalid";
}
System.out.println(type); // Weekend
// Arrow equivalent: case 6, 7 -> "Weekend";
```

